{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And fire came forth from HaShem.</b> The measure of the Holy One, blessed be He, is measure for measure. Korah sought a lofty rank that was not fitting for him, and in so doing came against HaShem, may He be blessed. Therefore he was punished with descent — he and those who supported him — as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded (Numbers 21:20): ״ומבמות הגיא״ — such was the affair of Korah, the father of all who exalt themselves and seek to seize authority unjustly. Also here in the punishment of burning there was measure for measure, for those two hundred and fifty men, who were firstborns, came to offer incense upon the fire with their firepans in their hands, and therefore they were punished with fire. And concerning them King David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 106:18): ״ותבער אש בעדתם להבה תלהט רשעים״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The citation Numbers 21:20 attaches to the phrase ומבמות הגיא, which appears in that verse; the proemistic association with Korah is the rabbinic derash referenced."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:20.093254023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}